                <pb facs="0233" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23534: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dyer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-30T12:00:00-07:23"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 3:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Sonora fears Carranza will send troops and establish military government
                    according to newspaper <hi rendition="#italic">La Nacion</hi> which says State
                    will not submit. Railroad men have given notice strike will be declared April
                    3rd.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dyer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
